   \\\"minLength\\\": 1\\n        },\\n        \\\"run\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"A command that reads test identifiers on stdin, one per line; its exit code is the verdict.\\\",\\n          \\\"minLength\\\": 1\\n        }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"checks\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"The tenant's own definition of done: a whole-tree check, as the tenant runs it locally. attavo build runs it each iteration, after the claims boundary, the criteria, and the selected tests -- pass requires its exit to be 0, and a non-zero exit reaches the executor as feedback. Optional; a tenant that declares none is not refused (unlike [tests], which build requires).\\\",\\n      \\\"additionalProperties\\\": false,\\n      \\\"required\\\": [\\\"command\\\"],\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"command\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The tenant's whole-tree check, run from the tenant root.\\\",\\n          \\\"minLength\\\": 1\\n        }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"forge\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"The tenant's own commit-status and issue-tracking reads. The product names no vendor: both keys are commands the tenant supplies. Optional; attavo verify refuses without checks_command, and attavo file-findings refuses without file_issue_command, but neither key requires the other.\\\",\\n      \\\"additionalProperties\\\": false,\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"checks_command\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Takes a full commit sha on argv; prints one line per check as \\\\\\\"<name> <conclusion>\\\\\\\". attavo verify runs it on the item's latest build record's sha before calling any adapter.\\\",\\n          \\\"minLength\\\": 1\\n        },\\n        \\\"file_issue_command\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Reads one finding as JSON on stdin and files it as a tenant issue. attavo file-findings runs it once per finding in the item's latest verify record.\\\",\\n          \\\"minLength\\\": 1\\n        }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"spec\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n      \\\"additionalProperties\\\": false,\\n      \\\"required\\\": [\\\"boundary\\\"],\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"boundary\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Which changes take the governed path. A change outside the boundary takes the tenant's ordinary pull-request flow, and the path ratio measures both.\\\",\\n          \\\"additionalProperties\\\": false,\\n          \\\"properties\\\": {\\n            \\\"paths\\\": {\\n              \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n              \\\"items\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"minLength\\\": 1},\\n              \\\"description\\\": \\\"Glob patterns; a change touching any of them is governed.\\\"\\n            },\\n            \\\"labels\\\": {\\n              \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n              \\\"items\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"minLength\\\": 1},\\n              \\\"description\\\": \\\"Issue labels; an issue carrying any of them is governed.\\\"\\n            },\\n            \\\"max_ordinary_lines\\\": {\\n              \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\",\\n              \\\"minimum\\\": 0,\\n              \\\"description\\\": \\\"A change above this many net lines is governed regardless of path or label.\\\"\\n            }\\n          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"gates\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Every gate the tenant runs, by name. The doctor's first proof is that each one rejects its fixture; a gate absent from this table does not exist.\\\",\\n      \\\"propertyNames\\\": {\\\"pattern\\\": \\\"^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$\\\"},\\n      \\\"additionalProperties\\\": {\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n        \\\"additionalProperties\\\": false,\\n        \\\"required\\\": [\\\"command\\\", \\\"retires\\\"],\\n        \\\"properties\\\": {\\n          \\\"command\\\": {\\n            \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n            \\\"description\\\": \\\"The script the gate runs, invoked with the tenant root as its working directory. Exit status is the verdict: non-zero rejects.\\\",\\n            \\\"minLength\\\": 1\\n          },\\n          \\\"retires\\\": {\\n            \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n            \\\"minItems\\\": 1,\\n            \\\"items\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"minLength\\\": 1},\\n            \\\"description\\\": \\\"What this gate replaced. A gate that retires nothing is not admitted to the table.\\\"\\n          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"paths\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n      \\\"additionalProperties\\\": false,\\n      \\\"required\\\": [\\\"specs\\\", \\\"records\\\", \\\"rulings\\\", \\\"rejections\\\"],\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"specs\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"minLength\\\": 1, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Directory of specs, one per work item, named by issue number.\\\"},\\n        \\\"rejections\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"minLength\\\": 1, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Directory of rejection fixtures, one subdirectory per gate name. The doctor's first proof runs each gate against its fixture and requires a rejection.\\\"},\\n        \\\"records\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"minLength\\\": 1, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Directory of records, append-only, one subdirectory per work item named by issue number. Scripts write every file here.\\\"},\\n        \\\"rulings\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"minLength\\\": 1, \\\"description\\\": \\\"The tenant's rulings file, rendered read-only; the merge of a proposed amendment is the ruling.\\\"}\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"operators\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n      \\\"additionalProperties\\\": false,\\n      \\\"required\\\": [\\\"approvers\\\"],\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"approvers\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n          \\\"items\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"minLength\\\": 1},\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Logins allowed to bind a spec's approval to a commit. `attavo approve` refuses a LOGIN not on this list.\\\"\\n        }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"doctor\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Optional; the doctor's own read. Absent, proof three's window starts at the install commit, as it always has.\\\",\\n      \\\"additionalProperties\\\": false,\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"from\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Anything git rev-parse --verify resolves to a commit on main's first-parent line, at or after the install commit -- a full or abbreviated sha, a tag, a ref -- where proof three's window starts. A tenant that adopted the product on a repository with pre-existing history names the commit after which every push arrived through the queue. Resolved and checked against main's first-parent line, not trusted: a spelling that does not resolve, or a commit that is not on that line, is refused by name.\\\",\\n          \\\"minLength\\\": 1\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"numLines\":183,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":183}}}\n+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cf9JhqBRdsntUfkE4VRPS\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I'll apply minimal, semantic-only edits to the manifest schema (add `drive` table), keeping the existing compact formatting style.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_c